WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.120
I want to continue in volume 5, picking up at June 16, 1903.

2
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.560
The heading says, "What renders the soul more dear, more beautiful, more lovable and

3
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:26.940
more intimate with God, is her perseverance in operating to please him alone."

4
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:33.100
Anyway my usual state, Louisa, said, "I found myself outside of myself, and I saw baby

5
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:39.340
Jesus with a cup full of bitterness and a stick in his hand.

6
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.760
And he said to me, 'See my daughter, what a cup of bitterness the world continuously

7
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.740
gives me to drink.'"

8
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:53.900
Now that cup of bitterness is total opposition of the human will to the divine will and all

9
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.340
the evils that follow with it.

10
00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:02.140
Louisa said, "Lord, share it with me so you won't suffer alone.

11
00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:07.720
So he gave me a drink to drink a little bit of that bitterness, and then with the stick

12
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:12.980
in his hand he began to pierce the place of my heart through, to the point of making

13
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:20.580
a whole, from which a rivelet of bitterness which I had drunk came out.

14
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:27.580
However, it was changed into sweet milk and went into the mouth of the baby and was all

15
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.340
sweetened and refreshed."

16
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:35.300
Now this sweet milk, which usually the Lord gives to her and indeed to other mystics

17
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:42.300
as well, is spiritual strengths and fortitude for all that they have to suffer.

18
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.820
And now because Louisa has taken the bitterness from him, in her it has been changed into

19
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.700
sweetness for him.

20
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:58.980
So this is what you call giving him a relief, it's one of the explanations of giving him

21
00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:05.660
a relief because the bitterness that she has suffered has made reparation for the sins

22
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:07.740
that are causing him grief.

23
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:14.020
The other explanation for relief is that we do something to save souls and that gives

24
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.340
him relief.

25
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:25.100
So the baby then was all sweetened and refreshed and he told me, "My daughter, when I give

26
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:34.100
the soul the bitterness of tribulations, if the soul conforms to the divine will, and

27
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:40.420
is grateful to me, which is the bit that we all find difficult, being grateful for sufferings,

28
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.820
and thanks me for it, and offers it to me as a gift.

29
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:53.260
For her it is bitterness, it is suffering, and for me it changes into sweetness and refreshment

30
00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.580
because he is receiving the opposite of what the world is giving to him.

31
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:02.180
This person is accepting the will of God, accepting suffering, accepting the cross and

32
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.540
offering it to him."

33
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.340
Jesus continued, "What cheers me the most and gives me the most pleasure is to see that

34
00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:20.860
the soul, whether she operates, that is works or suffers, is all intent on pleasing me alone."

35
00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:31.100
There is the issue and there is one of the many keys that's given to us in these writings

36
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:37.420
for us to test and see how well we're doing in our journey in the divine will.

37
00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:43.980
So I want to give you there, John 829, where Jesus said, "I only do what pleases him."

38
00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:53.380
So the only motivation that is acceptable from us trying to live the divine will is that

39
00:03:53.380 --> 00:04:02.260
of doing everything, everything, everything, just to please Jesus alone and for love of him.

40
00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:08.980
So he said, "What cheers me and gives me the most pleasure is to see somebody all intent

41
00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:13.780
on pleasing me alone with no other end or purpose of recompense."

42
00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.780
In other words, we're not looking to human beings to recompense.

43
00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:25.660
However, what renders the soul more dear, more beautiful, more lovable and more intimate

44
00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:30.180
with the divine being is her perseverance in this way of behaving.

45
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.900
You see, it's all right to do it once or twice or to remember it once a day or once

46
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:43.780
a week, but to actually live that way 24, 7, 3, 6, 5, that's what really glorifies God.

47
00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.820
With her perseverance in this way of behaving, which renders her immutable, that is immovable,

48
00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:58.300
unchangeable, like God, with the immutability of God.

49
00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:03.620
In fact, if today she does something and tomorrow she doesn't.

50
00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:09.420
If one time she has one end and another time another, if today she tries to please God and

51
00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:14.660
tomorrow she tries to please human beings, she is the image of one who today is a queen

52
00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.100
and tomorrow a most miserable servant.

53
00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.180
Today she nourishes herself with delicious food and tomorrow it felt.

54
00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:29.100
So he illustrates there that if we are one of these people that only serves God when

55
00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:34.660
we feel like it, then we are pitiable.

56
00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:41.620
Just a little while Jesus disappeared, but a little later he came back and he added.

57
00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:48.580
The sun is there for the benefit of all creatures on the planet, but not everyone enjoys these

58
00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.060
beneficial effects.

59
00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:58.660
In the same way, the sun gives its light to all, but who enjoys its beneficial effects?

60
00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:03.340
Surely it's the one who keeps his eyes open for the light of truth.

61
00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:13.140
Now Jesus is the truth, John 14, 6, I am the way, the truth and the life, and John 8, 32.

62
00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:20.420
All others, even if they are exposed to the sun remain in the dark, however, it is one

63
00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:27.660
who is all intent on pleasing me that truly enjoys and receives all the fondness of this

64
00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.660
sun.

65
00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:34.700
Now, this sun is that the sun in the sky is an image that Louisa gives continuously

66
00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.860
of Jesus because Jesus is the light of the world.

67
00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.220
And God himself is light, one John, one five, okay?

68
00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:51.860
So while the sun in the sky is there to benefit absolutely everybody, if people hide themselves

69
00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:57.580
in dark caves, they are not going to actually benefit from the sun whatsoever.

70
00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.180
If you pull down all your shutters and close your doors, you're not going to even let the

71
00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:05.500
light in, let alone the sunlight, so you won't benefit at all.

72
00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:11.780
It's the people go out and let themselves be exposed to the sunlight, who will get the

73
00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.180
warmth and all that goes with it.

74
00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:20.140
Now in the same way, we've got to open ourselves up to the Son of Justice, that is Jesus, and

75
00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:24.780
to the rays of his light, which are the truths that are actually coming to us, we've got

76
00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:31.940
to open ourselves up to that and let these actually change us, change our lives.

77
00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.060
So June the 30th, 1903.

78
00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:41.500
The Blessed Virgin teaches the soul how to keep her interior gaze fixed on Jesus.

79
00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:50.140
So you need to give yourself a heading for this and that's all eyes on Jesus.

80
00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:54.900
That was a motto of the church right from the very beginning, that if we keep all our

81
00:07:54.900 --> 00:08:02.780
eyes on Jesus, then everything that God wants to do with us can be done because the Son

82
00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:08.140
of God's justice and light and mercy is shining on our souls.

83
00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:14.100
So Louisa said, "I was outside of myself when I saw the Queen Mother, and prostrating myself

84
00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:19.060
at her feet, I said to her, 'My most sweet Mother, in what terrible constraints I find

85
00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:26.420
myself deprived of my only good and my very life, I feel I am touching the extremes.'

86
00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:31.020
While saying this I was crying and the most holy virgin opening herself up in the place

87
00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:38.140
of her heart, as if she were opening a tabernacle, took the baby from within it and gave him

88
00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.140
to me."

89
00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:47.580
Now there's one of the very wonderful icons of Blessed Mother that she is the tabernacle

90
00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.820
of the most high.

91
00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:55.660
And that's what we're meant to be also in a lesser extent.

92
00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:01.420
So that's 1 Corinthians 3, 16, "Know you not that you are the temple of the living God

93
00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:04.460
and that God dwells within you."

94
00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:10.500
So she said to Louisa, "My daughter, do not cry, she is the mother of all the living."

95
00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:19.020
As Jesus said in the Gospel of John, chapter 19, verse 25 to 26, "Mater, the mother of

96
00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.380
the whole church."

97
00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:27.900
My daughter, do not cry, "Here is your good, your life, and your all.

98
00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.740
It is Mary who gives us Jesus."

99
00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:36.740
That's one of the great doctrines of the church, because she brought the word incarnate down

100
00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.300
from heaven to the earth.

101
00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.920
She is the one who has brought us Jesus.

102
00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.900
She is the one who presented Jesus at his birth.

103
00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:47.740
She is the one who gives us the Redeemer at the cross.

104
00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:53.260
And she is the one who gives us our risen Lord as well.

105
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:57.300
And so she said, "Take him and keep him always with you.

106
00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:02.120
And as you keep him with him, keep your interior gaze fixed on him."

107
00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:09.340
That's two Corinthians 10, 5, St. Paul says that every thought must be captured and given

108
00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.380
to Christ.

109
00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:18.980
Do not be embarrassed if he does not tell you anything, or if you are unable to say anything.

110
00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.140
Just look at him in your interior.

111
00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.940
Now that's what contemplation is.

112
00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:27.740
I look at him and he looks at me.

113
00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:35.980
And by looking at him, you will understand everything and you will satisfy for all.

114
00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.220
Now she says, "You will."

115
00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:43.060
That means in doing this action, you will be able to do this when you think you're doing

116
00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.660
nothing.

117
00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.860
This is the beauty of the interior soul.

118
00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:57.620
And this is what the Lord wants from anyone wanting to live the divine will mystery and

119
00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:03.020
mission that we would have to be interior souls because all of the work of establishing

120
00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:06.580
the kingdom of God is within you.

121
00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:16.660
That's Luke 17, 21, that is the kingdom of God is within you.

122
00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.300
Now this is the beauty of the interior soul.

123
00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:25.580
Without voice, without education, there's no external thing that attracts her or upsets

124
00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:33.740
her, but all of her attraction, all of her goods are enclosed in her interior.

125
00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:40.020
By simply looking at Jesus, she easily understands everything and does everything.

126
00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:44.700
In this way, you will walk up to the top of Calvary.

127
00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.900
And once we, now notice she said, "You will walk."

128
00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.660
And then she says, "We will reach it.

129
00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.060
You're not alone.

130
00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.420
We will reach it.

131
00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.860
And you will no longer see him as a baby, but crucified.

132
00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:02.980
And you will remain crucified with him."

133
00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.660
That is full identification with Christ.

134
00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:17.020
That is what the Lord has been asking of Louisa from the very beginning that he wanted complete

135
00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:20.780
identification with her.

136
00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:28.400
She wanted him, he wanted her to have complete identification with him.

137
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.980
So it seemed that with the baby in my arms, and together with the most holy virgin, we

138
00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:41.100
walked Calvary, Jesus, Mary, and Louisa, a Trinity on earth.

139
00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:47.540
While walking, at times I would find someone who wanted to take Jesus away from me, and

140
00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:53.700
I would call on the Queen Mother for help, saying to her, "My mother helped me, for

141
00:12:53.700 --> 00:13:00.260
they wanted to snatch Jesus away from me, and she would answer me, 'Do not fear.

142
00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:06.060
Your care must be in keeping your interior gaze fixed on him.'"

143
00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:10.140
That's your two Corinthians 10, 5.

144
00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:17.460
This has so much power that all other powers, human and diabolical, remain debilitated and

145
00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.980
defeated.

146
00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:26.980
So Blessed Mother has here given us the method to have complete and total victory in the

147
00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:32.580
spiritual life, that if we keep our interior powers, that is the intellect, memory, and

148
00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:43.420
will, completely intent on Jesus, then nothing and nobody else can get through.

149
00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:48.740
But that takes an awful lot of self-denial and mortification on our part, and it means

150
00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:56.340
that we have to turn off televisions and gadgets and all kinds of stuff that feeds the influence

151
00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.300
of the world into our being.

152
00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:04.740
Now while we were walking, we found a temple in which holy mass was being celebrated.

153
00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.540
Now notice she doesn't say a church.

154
00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:13.860
At the time of Holy Communion, I flew to the altar with a baby in my arms in order to receive

155
00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:14.860
communion.

156
00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:19.340
But what was not my surprise when as soon as Jesus Christ entered me, he disappeared

157
00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.340
from my arms.

158
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.140
Of course, he has entered into her soul.

159
00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:28.740
Then after a little while, she said, "I was back to myself."

160
00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:32.540
So July the 3rd, 1903.

161
00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:41.060
If the soul gives herself completely to Jesus, now this is the issue.

162
00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:47.340
If the soul gives herself completely to Jesus in life, Jesus gives himself to her at her

163
00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.340
death.

164
00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:52.040
There's the exchange.

165
00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:59.700
And in the old liturgy, we used to say, "O admirabilé comercium, what an amarvelous exchange."

166
00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:05.580
So we give ourselves to Jesus during life and he gives himself to us in death.

167
00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:09.340
That means we have him eternally.

168
00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:13.780
And not only that, but you're exempted from purgatory.

169
00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:17.940
So this is one of the many messages we're given about purgatory that someone who truly

170
00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:23.940
genuinely lives in the divine will, 24, 7, 3, 6, 5, there is no purgatory.

171
00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:27.820
The purgatory is on earth.

172
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:33.540
This morning as I was very afflicted because of the loss of my adorable Jesus.

173
00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:40.220
All of a sudden, he made himself seen in my interior, filling my person completely.

174
00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:46.980
So I want to give you Galatians 2.20 there, "I no longer live, Christ lives in me."

175
00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:53.260
That is, completely means my head, my arms, and all the rest of my body.

176
00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:57.620
As I was seeing this, almost wanting to explain to me the meaning of the way he was

177
00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:05.020
making himself seen, he told me, "My daughter, why do you afflict yourself if I am the master

178
00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:09.660
of all of you, that is body, soul, and spirit?

179
00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:16.100
Okay, that's what it means to be in divine will, to live heaven on earth.

180
00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:22.460
When a soul comes to rendering me the master of her mind, of her arms, of her heart, and

181
00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:26.340
of her feet, sin cannot reign.

182
00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:31.340
Now that is 1 John 3, 2.

183
00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:38.500
And if something involuntary enters into her, since I am the master of the soul, and the

184
00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:46.980
soul is under the influence of my lordship, she is in continuous attitude of purgation.

185
00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:53.140
Now that means you are being purified continuously.

186
00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:58.660
And that's something immediately goes out of her, whatever it was that was trying to

187
00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.500
get in immediately goes out.

188
00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:07.620
Because if you are continuously in the divine will, the divine will makes absolutely certain

189
00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:11.060
that he preserves this union.

190
00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:17.340
And he is the one like a good farmer, pulling up a weed, the instant he sees it.

191
00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:25.140
Furthermore, since I am holy, it is difficult for her to retain within herself anything

192
00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.140
that's not holy.

193
00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:33.020
Now there I want you to put Leviticus 19, "You shall be holy, for I am holy," says

194
00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:34.020
the Lord.

195
00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:40.620
There's also a text in the Book of Amos, which I've just remembered right now, which

196
00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:46.540
says, "How can two walk together unless they be alike?"

197
00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:56.060
So if we are not holy like the Lord, then how can we possibly live this divine will?

198
00:17:56.060 --> 00:18:07.540
I'm also remembering Matthew chapter 5, and it's the very last paragraph in this chapter.

199
00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:20.980
So in my head it says it's something like 34 to 39 or 54 to 59 under which it is.

200
00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:28.900
But it says that you must be perfect like your heavenly father is perfect.

201
00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:35.860
And the quickest way to come to this perfection, perfect means complete whole, nothing missing.

202
00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:43.060
Okay, and the quickest way to do that, we're being told, is to keep our eyes completely

203
00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:47.940
fixed on Jesus and to keep our thoughts completely on him.

204
00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:55.380
So even more, Jesus says, "Since the soul has given all of herself to me in life, in

205
00:18:55.380 --> 00:19:01.960
justice, I will give all of myself to her in death, admitting her to the beatific vision

206
00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:04.340
without delay."

207
00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:11.100
Now this is actually an extraordinary statement because elsewhere Jesus says that nine out

208
00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:18.300
of ten people who die go to purgatory, therefore what is offered to the soul living in the divine

209
00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:22.040
will is completely extraordinary.

210
00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:27.940
But I want to give you Hebrews 12, 14, nothing unholy or unworthy can ever enter the presence

211
00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:35.060
of God and that means that if we stay completely at one with the Lord in the divine will, that

212
00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:41.540
we are sanctified and we are completely purged and he has explained how the purging happens,

213
00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:48.260
that if we stay in this union with him, that he doesn't allow anything to come in.

214
00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:51.220
So there's actually no need for purgatory.

215
00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:59.540
Victory is a severe mercy of God which allows people after death to be purified of things

216
00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:04.660
that they should have been purified of before death.

217
00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:12.260
So Jesus says, "If one gives herself completely to me, the flames of purgatory have nothing

218
00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:18.260
